britain is facing a migrant crisis  and this is thought to be the  government's answer  in what seems to be a pushback drill  jets appear to follow a boat  they eventually catch up with the vessel  and surround it  seemingly trying to turn it around or  escort it back through the waters  it appears to be a training exercise  but comes after french authorities  refused to entertain the idea of  pushbacks which would direct boats back  to french  water but as the home office refuses to  confirm  many want answers  repeatedly the home secretary has been  asked for answers on this issue of the  channel crossings of people who are  coming across the channel and i was in  dover myself  in recent weeks i know how really  fragile these craft are  a short time later the jet skis were  seen escorting what looked like are  boats carrying migrants  it's the latest of many  the waters are unsafe the boats aren't  fit for purpose and the task to cross  the busiest shipping lanes in the world  despite all the odds stacked against  them more than 14 000 migrants have made  the journey this year so far  a record figure up from 8417  last year  the home office says  we are seeing an unacceptable rise in  dangerous and unnecessary small boat  crossings that's why we continue to  explore all options available to bring  these numbers down  our primary focus is on preventing  people from entering the channel  tackling the criminal gangs responsible  and protecting lives  as part of our ongoing operational  response we continue to evaluate and  test a range of safe and legal options  for stopping small boats  but those with experience say pushbacks  should never be an option these vessels  are usually poorly constructed  overcrowded  many people don't have life jackets on  board  and they have very  no navigational aids whatsoever  and  the question i have is  if a pushback goes wrong and a vessel  capsizes as i uh nearly saw when i was  at lesvos  who is going to be held responsible  the home office say it will fix the  broken asylum system through its new  plan for immigration but until then  hundreds if not thousands more will  continue to make this perilous journey  shaman freeman powell sky news
 

